            <ArticleTitle>Two cases of coronary artery spasm induced by indocyanine green.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>877-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is no evidence in the literature that coronary artery spasm is induced by indocyanine green (ICG). In the present report, we describe 2 cases who developed chest pain with transient ST elevation on electrocardiograms after intravenous administration of ICG.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
